!!! The event loop.
!!!
!!! This replaces an accept-serve-close loop that handled one connection at a
!!! time. That shape is a development server: one client pausing mid-request
!!! stops every other client until it finishes or times out, and no amount of
!!! tuning changes it.
!!!
!!! What is here instead is nginx's shape rather than Apache's prefork, for a
!!! reason that is not a preference. The interpreter holds one stack, one heap
!!! and one set of globals, with no lock anywhere near them, and
!!! nil.std.threading offers `sleep`. A thread per connection is not available
!!! and will not be until the runtime is a different runtime. An event loop
!!! does not need one: poll says which sockets can be acted on, and one pass
!!! round the loop acts on each in turn.
!!!
!!! For more than one core, run more than one process over the same port --
!!! `share-port` below -- and let the kernel balance accepts between them.
!!!
!!! The application still owns dispatch. `pump` hands back one framed request
!!! at a time and `reply` takes the answer, so the routing, templates and
!!! sessions above are reached by the application's own paragraph. Matrix has
!!! no capturing closures, so a callback is not something this module could
!!! hold even if that were the nicer design.
!!!
!!! The engine is mutated in place. A record parameter in Matrix is a shared
!!! handle, and an array inside a record can be appended to and assigned
!!! element-wise, so holding a thousand connections costs a thousand slots
!!! rather than a copy of the whole table per event.

book nilweb.server.engine

read nil.std.core
read nil.std.net.socket
read nil.std.text
read nil.std.text.string_utils
read everything from nilweb.text.scan
read everything from nilweb.http.headers


!!! How long a connection may sit idle before it is closed.
!!!
!!! Two numbers, because the two risks differ. A connection that has sent
!!! nothing at all is probably a scan or a speculative socket a browser opened
!!! and forgot, and is worth little patience. One that is between requests on
!!! a keep-alive session is a real client thinking, and closing it early costs
!!! a handshake.
constant first-request-limit-ms as number is 10000
constant between-requests-limit-ms as number is 30000

!!! A request that arrives in pieces must finish within this, however slowly
!!! the pieces come. Without it, a client that sends one byte a second holds a
!!! slot indefinitely -- which is what slowloris is.
constant request-deadline-ms as number is 20000

!!! The most a request may be, header and body together. The cap stops the
!!! reading rather than rejecting afterwards.
constant request-limit as number is 1048576

!!! One read per pass. Large enough that an ordinary request arrives whole.
constant chunk-size as number is 65536

!!! How many requests one connection may serve before it is closed anyway.
!!! Not a safety limit -- a bound on how long any single connection can hold
!!! whatever it has accumulated, so a long-lived client cannot pin a slot for
!!! the life of the process.
constant keep-alive-limit as number is 1000


public connection begin record
    field handle as number
    !!! Request bytes read so far, waiting to be framed.
    field gathered as text
    !!! Response bytes not yet accepted by the socket.
    field outgoing as text
    !!! How much of `outgoing` has gone.
    field sent as number
    !!! Requests completed on this connection.
    field served as number
    field live as boolean
    !!! Whether to keep the connection after the response in flight.
    field keeping as boolean
    !!! When the current request started arriving, and when anything last did.
    field started-at as number
    field touched-at as number
    !!! Captured at accept, because by the time a response is logged the
    !!! socket may be closed and getpeername would fail. For the log only:
    !!! an address is not an identity, and behind a proxy it is the proxy's.
    field peer as text
end record


public engine begin record
    field listener as number
    field live as boolean
    field complaint as text
    field connections as array of connection
    field open-count as number
    field accepted-total as number
    field served-total as number
    field rejected-total as number
    field connection-limit as number
end record


!!! --- What one call to `pump` found.

public pumped begin record
    field found as boolean
    field handle as number
    field request as text
    !!! Whether the client asked to keep the connection open.
    field keep-alive as boolean
    !!! The peer's address, for the access log.
    field peer as text
end record


nothing-found returns pumped begin paragraph
    give build pumped with found being false, handle being 0, request being "",
        keep-alive being false, peer being ""
end paragraph


!!! --- Bind a port and prepare to serve.
!!!
!!! `limit` is how many connections may be open at once. A ceiling rather than
!!! none, because every open connection holds its accumulated request text,
!!! and a server that accepts without limit is a server that can be asked to
!!! hold more than it has memory for.

public start-engine receives host as text, port as number, limit as number returns engine begin paragraph
    variable connections as array of connection is []
    value opened is nil.std.net::listen with host being host, port being port, backlog being 512
    consider opened
        when Result.Error holding why then
            give build engine with listener being 0, live being false, complaint being why,
                connections being connections, open-count being 0, accepted-total being 0,
                served-total being 0, rejected-total being 0, connection-limit being limit
        when Result.Ok holding handle then begin block
            !!! The listener does not block: poll has already said a connection
            !!! is pending, and a blocking accept that then found none --
            !!! because the peer withdrew in between -- would stop the loop on
            !!! behalf of one socket.
            evaluate nil.std.net::set_blocking with handle being handle, blocking being false
            evaluate nil.std.net::watch with handle being handle, flags being nil.std.net::ready_readable
            give build engine with listener being handle, live being true, complaint being "",
                connections being connections, open-count being 0, accepted-total being 0,
                served-total being 0, rejected-total being 0, connection-limit being limit
        end block
        otherwise
            give build engine with listener being 0, live being false,
                complaint being "the port could not be bound", connections being connections,
                open-count being 0, accepted-total being 0, served-total being 0,
                rejected-total being 0, connection-limit being limit
    end consider
end paragraph


!!! --- Let other processes bind the same port, for running on more than one
!!! core. Opt-in, because switched on by accident it would split traffic with
!!! a stray server rather than failing to start.

public share-port receives server as engine returns boolean begin paragraph
    when not server.live then
        give false
    end when
    value outcome is nil.std.net::set_reuse_port with handle being server.listener, enabled being true
    consider outcome
        when Result.Ok holding amount then give true
        otherwise give false
    end consider
end paragraph


public stop-engine receives server as engine returns nothing begin paragraph
    repeat for each held in server.connections
        when held.live then
            evaluate nil.std.net::unwatch with handle being held.handle
            evaluate nil.std.net::close with handle being held.handle
        end when
    end repeat
    when server.live then
        evaluate nil.std.net::unwatch with handle being server.listener
        evaluate nil.std.net::close with handle being server.listener
    end when
    set server.live to false
    give nothing
end paragraph


!!! --- One pass: wait for readiness, act on everything ready, and hand back
!!! the first framed request found.
!!!
!!! A pass may frame several requests. Only one is returned, and the rest stay
!!! in their connections' buffers to be found by the next call -- which is why
!!! `pump` checks for an already-framed request before it waits at all. The
!!! alternative, returning a list, would be an array crossing back and forth
!!! for no gain.

public pump receives server as engine, timeout as number returns pumped begin paragraph
    when not server.live then
        give nothing-found with nothing
    end when

    !!! Something framed on an earlier pass and not yet handed over.
    value already is first-framed with server being server
    when already.found then
        give already
    end when

    value counted is nil.std.net::wait with timeout_milliseconds being timeout
    consider counted
        when Result.Error holding why then begin block
            set server.complaint to why
            give nothing-found with nothing
        end block
        otherwise set server.complaint to ""
    end consider

    variable draining as boolean is true
    repeat while draining
        value packed is nil.std.net::next_ready with nothing
        consider packed
            when Result.Ok holding ready then begin block
                when ready equals 0 then
                    set draining to false
                end when
                when ready is greater than 0 then
                    evaluate act-on with server being server, ready being ready
                end when
            end block
            otherwise set draining to false
        end consider
    end repeat

    give first-framed with server being server
end paragraph


act-on receives server as engine, ready as number returns nothing begin paragraph
    value handle is nil.std.net::ready_handle with packed being ready
    when handle equals server.listener then
        evaluate take-connections with server being server
        give nothing
    end when

    value slot is slot-of with server being server, handle being handle
    when slot is less than 0 then
        !!! Readiness for a connection this engine no longer tracks. Unwatch
        !!! rather than guess: the handle may since have been reissued.
        evaluate nil.std.net::unwatch with handle being handle
        give nothing
    end when

    when nil.std.net::is_writable with packed being ready then
        evaluate push-outgoing with server being server, slot being slot
    end when
    !!! Readable and finished can both be set: a peer that hung up may still
    !!! have sent something, and that something is read before the connection
    !!! is dropped or the last request of a session is lost.
    when nil.std.net::is_readable with packed being ready then
        evaluate pull-incoming with server being server, slot being slot
    end when
    when nil.std.net::is_finished with packed being ready then
        value held is server.connections at slot
        when held.live and (nil.std.text::length with s being held.outgoing) equals held.sent then
            evaluate drop with server being server, slot being slot
        end when
    end when
    give nothing
end paragraph


!!! --- Accept until the listener says there is nothing pending.
!!!
!!! Poll reports a listener readable once however many connections are
!!! waiting, so a loop that accepted one per pass would fall behind under load
!!! and never catch up.

take-connections receives server as engine returns nothing begin paragraph
    variable accepting as boolean is true
    repeat while accepting
        value taken is nil.std.net::accept with handle being server.listener
        consider taken
            when Result.Ok holding client then begin block
                when client equals 0 then
                    set accepting to false
                end when
                when client is greater than 0 then
                    evaluate admit with server being server, client being client
                end when
            end block
            when Result.Error holding why then begin block
                set server.complaint to why
                set accepting to false
            end block
            otherwise set accepting to false
        end consider
    end repeat
    give nothing
end paragraph


admit receives server as engine, client as number returns nothing begin paragraph
    set server.accepted-total to server.accepted-total plus 1
    when server.open-count is at least server.connection-limit then
        !!! At the ceiling. Closed immediately rather than queued: a queue
        !!! here is memory held on behalf of a client that is already being
        !!! refused, and a refusal it can see is better than a stall it cannot.
        set server.rejected-total to server.rejected-total plus 1
        evaluate nil.std.net::close with handle being client
        give nothing
    end when

    !!! Non-blocking, so neither a slow sender nor a slow reader can hold the
    !!! loop. Reads go through receive, which tells "nothing yet" apart from
    !!! "the peer closed"; writes go out through send_some as the socket takes
    !!! them.
    evaluate nil.std.net::set_blocking with handle being client, blocking being false
    evaluate nil.std.net::set_no_delay with handle being client, enabled being true
    evaluate nil.std.net::watch with handle being client, flags being nil.std.net::ready_readable

    value now-at is now in milliseconds
    value free-slot is dead-slot-of with server being server
    value fresh is build connection with handle being client, gathered being "", outgoing being "",
        sent being 0, served being 0, live being true, keeping being true,
        started-at being now-at, touched-at being now-at,
        peer being (peer-of with handle being client)
    when free-slot is at least 0 then
        set server.connections at free-slot to fresh
    otherwise
        append fresh to server.connections
    end when
    set server.open-count to server.open-count plus 1
    give nothing
end paragraph


pull-incoming receives server as engine, slot as number returns nothing begin paragraph
    value held is server.connections at slot
    when not held.live then
        give nothing
    end when

    value counted is nil.std.net::receive with handle being held.handle, maximum_bytes being chunk-size
    consider counted
        when Result.Error holding why then begin block
            evaluate drop with server being server, slot being slot
            give nothing
        end block
        when Result.Ok holding amount then begin block
            !!! Minus one is "nothing yet" -- a spurious wakeup, or a peer
            !!! that stopped mid-send. Not a close, and dropping the
            !!! connection here is the bug this distinction exists to prevent.
            when amount is less than 0 then
                give nothing
            end when
            when amount equals 0 then
                evaluate drop with server being server, slot being slot
                give nothing
            end when
            value arrived is nil.std.net::received with nothing
            consider arrived
                when Result.Ok holding piece then
                    evaluate absorb with server being server, slot being slot, piece being piece
                otherwise
                    evaluate drop with server being server, slot being slot
            end consider
        end block
        otherwise evaluate drop with server being server, slot being slot
    end consider
    give nothing
end paragraph


absorb receives server as engine, slot as number, piece as text returns nothing begin paragraph
    value held is server.connections at slot
    value whole is held.gathered plus piece
    value now-at is now in milliseconds
    when (nil.std.text::length with s being whole) is greater than request-limit then
        !!! Refused by closing rather than by answering 413: the request is
        !!! still arriving, and a response written into a stream the client is
        !!! still filling is a response it may never read.
        evaluate drop with server being server, slot being slot
        give nothing
    end when
    set server.connections at slot to build connection with handle being held.handle,
        gathered being whole, outgoing being held.outgoing, sent being held.sent,
        served being held.served, live being true, keeping being held.keeping,
        started-at being held.started-at, touched-at being now-at, peer being held.peer
    give nothing
end paragraph


!!! --- The first connection holding a complete request.

first-framed receives server as engine returns pumped begin paragraph
    variable index as number is 0
    repeat while index is less than the length of server.connections
        value held is server.connections at index
        value waiting is held.live and (nil.std.text::length with s being held.outgoing) equals held.sent
        when waiting and not (held.gathered equals "") then
            when request-is-complete with message being held.gathered then
                give build pumped with found being true, handle being held.handle,
                    request being held.gathered,
                    keep-alive being (wants-keep-alive with message being held.gathered),
                    peer being held.peer
            end when
        end when
        set index to index plus 1
    end repeat
    give nothing-found with nothing
end paragraph


!!! --- Answer a request and either keep the connection or close it.
!!!
!!! The response is handed over whole and sent as the socket takes it. A
!!! client that reads slowly holds its own buffer and nobody else's.

public reply receives server as engine, handle as number, response as text, keep-open as boolean
    returns nothing begin paragraph
    value slot is slot-of with server being server, handle being handle
    when slot is less than 0 then
        give nothing
    end when
    value held is server.connections at slot
    value now-at is now in milliseconds
    value more-allowed is held.served plus 1 is less than keep-alive-limit
    set server.connections at slot to build connection with handle being handle,
        gathered being "", outgoing being response, sent being 0,
        served being held.served plus 1, live being true,
        keeping being keep-open and more-allowed,
        started-at being now-at, touched-at being now-at, peer being held.peer
    set server.served-total to server.served-total plus 1
    evaluate push-outgoing with server being server, slot being slot
    give nothing
end paragraph


!!! --- Send what the socket will take, and decide what happens next.

push-outgoing receives server as engine, slot as number returns nothing begin paragraph
    value held is server.connections at slot
    when not held.live then
        give nothing
    end when
    value width is nil.std.text::length with s being held.outgoing
    when width equals held.sent then
        give nothing
    end when

    value sent is nil.std.net::send_some with handle being held.handle,
        data being held.outgoing, offset being held.sent
    consider sent
        when Result.Error holding why then begin block
            !!! The peer left before its answer arrived. An ordinary Tuesday,
            !!! not an error in the program.
            evaluate drop with server being server, slot being slot
            give nothing
        end block
        when Result.Ok holding amount then begin block
            value moved is when amount is less than 0 give 0 otherwise give amount end when
            value now-sent is held.sent plus moved
            value now-at is now in milliseconds
            set server.connections at slot to build connection with handle being held.handle,
                gathered being held.gathered, outgoing being held.outgoing, sent being now-sent,
                served being held.served, live being true, keeping being held.keeping,
                started-at being held.started-at, touched-at being now-at, peer being held.peer
            when now-sent is less than width then
                !!! More to go. Watch for writability so the next pass carries
                !!! on, rather than spinning on a socket that is full.
                evaluate nil.std.net::watch with handle being held.handle,
                    flags being nil.std.net::ready_writable
                give nothing
            end when
            evaluate finish-response with server being server, slot being slot
        end block
        otherwise evaluate drop with server being server, slot being slot
    end consider
    give nothing
end paragraph


finish-response receives server as engine, slot as number returns nothing begin paragraph
    value held is server.connections at slot
    when not held.keeping then
        evaluate drop with server being server, slot being slot
        give nothing
    end when
    !!! Kept open for another request: clear the response, read again.
    value now-at is now in milliseconds
    set server.connections at slot to build connection with handle being held.handle,
        gathered being "", outgoing being "", sent being 0, served being held.served,
        live being true, keeping being true, started-at being now-at, touched-at being now-at,
        peer being held.peer
    evaluate nil.std.net::watch with handle being held.handle, flags being nil.std.net::ready_readable
    give nothing
end paragraph


drop receives server as engine, slot as number returns nothing begin paragraph
    value held is server.connections at slot
    when not held.live then
        give nothing
    end when
    evaluate nil.std.net::unwatch with handle being held.handle
    evaluate nil.std.net::close with handle being held.handle
    set server.connections at slot to build connection with handle being 0, gathered being "",
        outgoing being "", sent being 0, served being 0, live being false, keeping being false,
        started-at being 0, touched-at being 0, peer being ""
    set server.open-count to server.open-count minus 1
    give nothing
end paragraph


!!! --- Close connections that have stopped making progress.
!!!
!!! Called by the application between passes. Three deadlines, because the
!!! three cases differ: a connection that has said nothing is probably a scan,
!!! one that is mid-request may be slowloris, and one between keep-alive
!!! requests is a real client thinking. Gives back how many were closed.

public sweep-idle receives server as engine returns number begin paragraph
    value now-at is now in milliseconds
    variable closed as number is 0
    variable index as number is 0
    repeat while index is less than the length of server.connections
        value held is server.connections at index
        when held.live then
            value quiet-for is now-at minus held.touched-at
            value arriving-for is now-at minus held.started-at
            value nothing-yet is held.gathered equals "" and held.served equals 0
            value mid-request is not (held.gathered equals "")
            value over-first is nothing-yet and quiet-for is greater than first-request-limit-ms
            value over-deadline is mid-request and arriving-for is greater than request-deadline-ms
            value over-between is held.served is greater than 0 and held.gathered equals ""
                and quiet-for is greater than between-requests-limit-ms
            when over-first or over-deadline or over-between then
                evaluate drop with server being server, slot being index
                set closed to closed plus 1
            end when
        end when
        set index to index plus 1
    end repeat
    give closed
end paragraph


!!! --- Whether the client asked to keep the connection.
!!!
!!! HTTP/1.1 keeps it unless Connection says close; HTTP/1.0 closes unless
!!! Connection says keep-alive. Getting this backwards for 1.0 is how a
!!! server ends up holding connections no client will ever use again.

public wants-keep-alive receives message as text returns boolean begin paragraph
    value head is head-of with message being message
    value stated is nil.std.text::to_lower with s being
        (field-in with head being head, name being "Connection")
    value first-line is before-first with input being head, separator being newline
    value old-version is nil.std.text::contains with s being first-line, needle being "HTTP/1.0"
    when nil.std.text::contains with s being stated, needle being "close" then
        give false
    end when
    when old-version then
        give nil.std.text::contains with s being stated, needle being "keep-alive"
    end when
    give true
end paragraph


field-in receives head as text, name as text returns text begin paragraph
    value lines is split-on with input being head, separator being newline
    repeat for each line in lines
        value trimmed is nil.std.text::trim with s being line
        value found is nil.std.text::trim with s being (before-first with input being trimmed, separator being ":")
        when same-folded with left being found, right being name then
            give nil.std.text::trim with s being (after-first with input being trimmed, separator being ":")
        end when
    end repeat
    give ""
end paragraph


head-of receives message as text returns text begin paragraph
    value marker is (crlf with nothing) plus (crlf with nothing)
    value cut is nil.std.text::index_of with s being message, needle being marker
    when cut is at least 0 then
        give nil.std.text::substring with s being message, start being 0, length being cut
    end when
    value loose is nil.std.text::index_of with s being message, needle being newline plus newline
    when loose is at least 0 then
        give nil.std.text::substring with s being message, start being 0, length being loose
    end when
    give message
end paragraph


!!! --- Whether enough of the message has arrived to answer it.
!!!
!!! The header section ends at the first blank line. After that a body is
!!! expected only if Content-Length says so. Chunked transfer encoding is not
!!! accepted, and a request asking for it is answered by the layer above
!!! rather than waited on here.

public request-is-complete receives message as text returns boolean begin paragraph
    value marker is (crlf with nothing) plus (crlf with nothing)
    variable head-length as number is nil.std.text::index_of with s being message, needle being marker
    variable separator as number is 4
    when head-length is less than 0 then
        set head-length to nil.std.text::index_of with s being message, needle being newline plus newline
        set separator to 2
    end when
    when head-length is less than 0 then
        give false
    end when

    value head is nil.std.text::substring with s being message, start being 0, length being head-length
    value declared is digits-value with digits being (field-in with head being head, name being "Content-Length")
    when declared is at most 0 then
        give true
    end when
    value body-start is head-length plus separator
    give ((nil.std.text::length with s being message) minus body-start) is at least declared
end paragraph


!!! --- A decimal count, without borrowing a parser that raises on bad input.
!!! Anything that is not all digits is zero: a Content-Length a client made up
!!! must not be able to stop the server with a fault.

digits-value receives digits as text returns number begin paragraph
    value width is nil.std.text::length with s being digits
    when width is less than 1 or width is greater than 18 then
        give 0
    end when
    variable total as number is 0
    variable index as number is 0
    repeat while index is less than width
        value code is nil.std.text::byte_at with s being digits, index being index
        when code is less than 48 or code is greater than 57 then
            give 0
        end when
        set total to (total times 10) plus (code minus 48)
        set index to index plus 1
    end repeat
    give total
end paragraph


slot-of receives server as engine, handle as number returns number begin paragraph
    variable index as number is 0
    repeat while index is less than the length of server.connections
        value held is server.connections at index
        when held.live and held.handle equals handle then
            give index
        end when
        set index to index plus 1
    end repeat
    give 0 minus 1
end paragraph


!!! --- A slot whose connection has closed, so the table is reused rather than
!!! growing once per connection for the life of the process.

dead-slot-of receives server as engine returns number begin paragraph
    variable index as number is 0
    repeat while index is less than the length of server.connections
        when not (server.connections at index).live then
            give index
        end when
        set index to index plus 1
    end repeat
    give 0 minus 1
end paragraph


!!! --- Where the server can be reached, for the line printed at startup.

!!! --- The peer's address, or "" when it cannot be read.
!!! Never a decision, only a log line.

peer-of receives handle as number returns text begin paragraph
    value found is nil.std.net::peer_address with handle being handle
    consider found
        when Result.Ok holding shown then give shown
        otherwise give ""
    end consider
end paragraph


public address-text receives host as text, port as number returns text begin paragraph
    value shown is when host equals "" give "0.0.0.0" otherwise give host end when
    give "http://" plus shown plus ":" plus (port becomes text) plus "/"
end paragraph
